    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (25 tests, 0 failures/errors), including the two new `Cp15Tests` and all pre-existing tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field on the owner response so it returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing pattern used for the other computed fields (`membershipNumber`, `initials`, `displayName`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` string property (readOnly) to the Owner response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression backed by a `membershipTier(owner)` helper that returns `\"SILVER\"` only when `namesakeCount == 0` (guarding null for seed data) and the email is present (non-null, non-blank), else `\"BRONZE\"`.\n\nThe tier is derived at mapping time from the entity's already-computed `namesakeCount` and `email`, so it stays consistent on both the create response and subsequent `GET /owners/{id}` reads.",
